    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0389" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-21T13:00:00+09:00">October 21, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 21—3:52 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>192. Embassy’s 191, October 21, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d268-f1"/> I
                    delivered the note<anchor n="2" xml:id="d268-f2"/> this morning in person. The
                    Minister for Foreign affairs read it and <pb facs="0390" n="280" xml:id="pg280"
                    /> said that its tone was sympathetic and he desired once again to express his
                    appreciation [of] the considerate attitude of the United States. He said that
                    conditions in Manchuria seemed to be improving and that he was hopeful about it.
                    He insisted that there was no likelihood of war and that Japan was prepared to
                    negotiate with China at any time.</p>
                <p>It is difficult to realize the determination of the Japanese public to have no
                    interference by the parties in Manchuria. No government would dare to admit it
                    unless well camouflaged. Shidehara has been put to great straits to prove to the
                    powers that there was no war and no danger of one and to the Japanese public
                    that their rights were being adequately protected and that there has been no
                    outside interference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
